    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.9/p@172825",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "KING HENRY.\nThus stands my state, ’twixt Cade and York distressed,\nLike to a ship that, having scaped a tempest,\nIs straightway calmed and boarded with a pirate.\nBut now is Cade driven back, his men dispersed,\nAnd now is York in arms to second him.\nI pray thee, Buckingham, go and meet him,\nAnd ask him what’s the reason of these arms.\nTell him I’ll send Duke Edmund to the Tower.—\nAnd, Somerset, we will commit thee thither,\nUntil his army be dismissed from him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.9/p@172825/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 11,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
